From: ArtisanROM x1s fork
Subject: [PATCH] exynos990: import Samsung's 2025 OSRC security fixes

The Galaxy S20 stopped receiving updates in 2023, but the S20 FE
(SM-G780F, also Exynos 990) got security releases until October 2025.
These are the driver fixes Samsung shipped in the G780FXXSOFYJ1 kernel
source (opensource.samsung.com), as imported by LineageOS in
android_kernel_samsung_universal9830 commit fda5811c2, limited to drivers
this kernel actually builds (Mali bv_r38p1 only; the unused bv_r32p1 copy
and the Qualcomm qca6390 Wi-Fi driver are left out):

- mali bv_r38p1: wait for pending page/bus/GPU fault workers before a
  terminating context gives up its address space (use-after-free), tear
  down aliased imports with their real physical pages, and only build a
  2 MB level-2 entry when 512 pages are really mapped.
- uvcvideo: skip frames of type UVC_VS_UNDEFINED (CVE-2024-53104, used in
  the wild to unlock seized Android phones over USB), reject units with
  ID 0 or duplicate IDs, and refuse format descriptors shorter than 4
  bytes.
- hid-input: reject out-of-range keycodes in hidinput_setkeycode().
- hid-multitouch: drop feature reports whose report ID does not match.
- exynos-iommu: take a page reference only for PFNs backed by a struct
  page instead of trusting the VMA's PFNMAP flag.
- cpif: bound the perftest sysfs mode/session/cpu values.
- vision: clear dma_buf/format pointers after release (double free).

The UVC hunk is adapted: this tree lacked the "buflen < 4" check that the
S20 FE source already had, so it is added here as well.

